==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɪndəl|s=2}}
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|bĭnʹdl|bĭnʹdəl}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪndl/}},<ref name="OED2"/> {{IPAchar|/ˈbɪndəl/}},<ref name="OED2"/>
* {{audio|en|En-au-bindle.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰendʰ-}}
{{unk|en}}; compare {{cog|ang|bindele||a binding, a tying}}<ref name="OED1">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50022232 ˈbindle¹]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref> from {{m|ang|bindan||to bind}}, and {{m|en|bundle}}. Additionally, compare {{m|en|mister}} from {{m|en|master}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|now|_|Scottish}}<ref name="OED1"/> Any given [[length]] of [[cord]], [[rope]], [[twine]], etc, used to [[bind]] something.<ref name="OED1"/>

===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰendʰ-}}
[[File:Hobos2.jpg|thumb|The front [[hobo]] carries a '''bindle''' on the end of a stick.]]
[[File:Flavcocaine.jpg|thumb|Several '''bindles''' of [[cocaine]]]]
Probably a corruption of {{m|en|bundle}}; perhaps influenced by the preceding word ''bindle'' meaning "length of cord used to bind something".<ref name="OED2">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50022233 bindle²]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|and|Canada|_|slang}} A [[bundle]] carried by a [[hobo]] (usually containing his possessions), often on a stick slung over the shoulder; a [[blanket roll]].<ref name="OED2"/>
#* {{RQ:McCarthy The Road|passage={{...}}lastly he made a '''bindle''' in a plastic tarp of some cans of juice and cans of fruit and cans of vegetables {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|US|and|Canada|_|slang}} Any bundle or [[package]]; specifically one containing [[narcotic]]s such as [[cocaine]], [[heroin]], or [[morphine]].<ref name="OED2"/>

